    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to generate offensive momentum today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who represents our clear standout play with a score of 76.60. While facing the difficult arm of Woo, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from hitting second in the order and a favorable park factor, which helps neutralize the pitcher's skill set. **Kyle Tucker** (68.81) and **Andy Pages** (64.76) also project as strong starts against Keller. **Andy Pages** in particular gets a nice efficiency boost from his prime spot in the batting order, allowing him to capitalize on early-game scoring opportunities despite a neutral platoon matchup.\n\nNavigating the deeper end of our roster, **Liam Hicks** (59.93) and **Josh Jung** (59.71) fall into the high-end marginal category, hovering just below our \"strong\" start threshold. **Liam Hicks** is a fascinating case today; while his raw base projection is modest, his leadoff placement and a +19% boost from facing Kelly drive his score upward, making him a high-upside play if he can capitalize on the elevated volume of plate appearances. Conversely, **Coby Mayo** (42.53) remains our most precarious start. His profile is heavily hampered by an 8th-order slot and a negative platoon split against Woo, though the favorable park environment prevents him from dipping below the replacement floor. With stars like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg** currently unavailable due to off-days or IL stints, our depth is being tested. **Liam Hicks** ultimately edged out our other bench options due to that critical leadoff positioning, which is vital in 5x5 Roto formats where maximizing total volume remains a priority to keep pace in the standings.",
